content.text:
Readable text often benefits from a limit on how wide a content region can grow:

```css
.article {
  max-width: 65ch;
}
```

You do not need to memorize the number 65.

The idea is that a content region can stop growing when extra width would make reading harder.

target.css:
.viewport-shell { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; padding: 20px; background: #0f172a; min-height: 200px; }
.callout-card { width: 100%; max-width: 320px; padding: 16px; border-radius: 10px; border: 1px solid #38bdf8; background: #1e293b; color: #f8fafc; }
.callout-card h2 { margin: 0 0 8px 0; font-size: 16px; color: #38bdf8; }
.callout-card p { margin: 0; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.5; color: #cbd5e1; }

